    "insert": "\nEnsure the provisional title aligns with the theme and purpose of the exposé, while being creative and specific. The title should represent the focus on integrating AI into healthcare workflows, be engaging and avoid being overly generic.\nThe title is functional and accurately describes the topic but could be more creative and could benefit from more engaging language while remaining concise and suitable. The current title might be too technical, potentially not invoking the readers interest.\nExperiment with alternative phrasings, or introduce action verbs or metaphors. Capture the essence of optimizing collaboration between AI and clinicians.\n\nPresent a compelling and focused introduction to captivate the audience. The hook should immediatly highlight why the collaboration between AI and clinicians is both timely and transformative.\nThe opening mentions the increasing importance of AI but lacks a striking hook. You could use real world examples, like AI successfully detecting a rare disease faster than human doctors, to intrigue readers. Generic or overly broad openings fail to establish immediate relevance.\nReframe the hook to include a striking example or question. It should indicate possible conflicts. Reflect on whether the hook connects logically to the research questions.\n\nProvide a detailed description of the challenges of providing a framework for AI integration into healthcare. Clearly articulate why solving the problem matters for the society.\nThe exposé addresses the problem broadly, mentioning ethical concerns and workflow inefficiencies but does not elaborate specific scenarios or consequences. For example radiologists are struggling to trust AI generated imaging analysis, due to its intransparent process. A thorough problem description helps to understand its implications. Without concrete examples, the problem might seem too abstract.\nUse examples from healthcare, such as ethical dilemmas that could arise from evaluating AI outputs. Reference the problem description with recent research or case studies to ensure depth.\n\nClearly define the healthcare environment and stakeholders affected by AI integration. The exposé should specify the relevant area of healthcare such as radiology or diagnostics.\nThe exposé mentions radiology and treatment planning, but doesn't explore specific details. Be specific to be focused, but broad enough to solve interconnecting problems at this scope.\nList the relevant stakeholder like clinicians, patients or administrators. Align the domain to account them at the research questions.\n\nSummarize existing approaches and identify their limitations. Clearly articulate the gaps in current frameworks.\nThe exposé identifies challenges like limited validation and interpretability but lacks specifics on current tools or frameworks. Criticism must directly support the argument for the proposed research.\nOutline the SOTA in one sentence to base the research questions ontheir  current research gaps.\n\nEnsure the research questions are clear, focused and actionable. The questions should directly address the identified problems and align with the framework.\nThe questions are clear but could specify measurable outcomes or methodologies. For example rephrasing to \"How does an AI/Human collaboration framework enhance diagnostic accuracy?\" provides a measurable unit for quantitative analysis against competing solutions. The questions must be researchable within the time frame of a beachlor thesis. With vague or overly broad questions you could lost your research focus and miss the time schedule.\nRefine the questions ensuring they directly link to the stated problem. Choose a specific topic, so that the research area doesn't become too large.\n\n"
